1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,069
Is the Caspian Sea really a sea?

2
00:00:02,419 --> 00:00:05,565
The Caspian sits between Europe and Asia,

3
00:00:05,565 --> 00:00:10,399
surrounded by five countries: Russia, Kazakhstan, Turkmenistan,

4
00:00:10,399 --> 00:00:11,934
Iran and Azerbaijan.

5
00:00:12,284 --> 00:00:15,291
It covers about three hundred seventy thousand

6
00:00:15,291 --> 00:00:18,429
square kilometers. That's bigger than Japan, and

7
00:00:18,429 --> 00:00:20,848
it makes the Caspian the largest lake

8
00:00:20,848 --> 00:00:21,436
on Earth.

9
00:00:21,786 --> 00:00:24,793
Why a lake? Because it's completely surrounded

10
00:00:24,793 --> 00:00:27,276
by land, with no natural connection to

11
00:00:27,276 --> 00:00:27,930
the ocean.

12
00:00:28,280 --> 00:00:30,074
So why call it a sea? Its

13
00:00:30,074 --> 00:00:32,370
water is salty, about a third as

14
00:00:32,370 --> 00:00:34,595
salty as the ocean, and it's so

15
00:00:34,595 --> 00:00:36,963
big that it has waves, storms and

16
00:00:36,963 --> 00:00:37,752
even seals.

17
00:00:38,102 --> 00:00:40,244
Millions of years ago, it was part

18
00:00:40,244 --> 00:00:42,386
of an ancient ocean. When the land

19
00:00:42,386 --> 00:00:44,779
rose around it, the water was trapped.

20
00:00:45,129 --> 00:00:48,395
The name matters. Under international law, seas

21
00:00:48,395 --> 00:00:51,314
and lakes are divided differently, and the

22
00:00:51,314 --> 00:00:54,024
Caspian floor holds huge amounts of oil

23
00:00:54,024 --> 00:00:54,580
and gas.

24
00:00:54,930 --> 00:00:57,674
In 2018, the five countries signed an

25
00:00:57,674 --> 00:01:00,715
agreement giving it a special status, not

26
00:01:00,715 --> 00:01:02,718
quite a sea and not quite a

27
00:01:02,718 --> 00:01:05,981
lake. Its surface is also about twenty-eight

28
00:01:05,981 --> 00:01:07,687
meters below sea level.

29
00:01:08,037 --> 00:01:10,977
The Caspian is also famous for sturgeon,

30
00:01:10,977 --> 00:01:14,064
ancient fish whose eggs become caviar, one

31
00:01:14,064 --> 00:01:16,563
of the most expensive foods in the

32
00:01:16,563 --> 00:01:19,944
world. Overfishing has made many wild sturgeon

33
00:01:19,944 --> 00:01:20,752
endangered.

34
00:01:21,102 --> 00:01:24,238
The Volga, Europe's longest river, brings most

35
00:01:24,238 --> 00:01:26,898
of the Caspian's water. And because the

36
00:01:26,898 --> 00:01:30,239
lake is slowly shrinking, scientists are watching

37
00:01:30,239 --> 00:01:31,534
its future closely.

38
00:01:31,884 --> 00:01:33,532
So what do you think: sea or

39
00:01:33,532 --> 00:01:35,297
lake? Tell me in the comments.

